-- EQUIL_1D_COMPVD_WATER_GASCAP_SWATINIT with endpoint scaling: every cell
-- has its own connate (SWL) and critical (SWCR) water, and its own minimum
-- (SGL) and maximum (SGU) gas.  SWATINIT is unchanged, so the endpoints
-- alone decide how each cell takes its SWATINIT water.
--
-- Gas cap (1-24): in 1-4 SWATINIT lies between SWL and SWCR, in 9-12 it
-- equals SWL, in 13-16 it lies below SWL, and in 17-20 above SWCR.  Cells
-- 5-8 have SGU 0.80, below 1 - SWL.  Oil zone (25-34): SWL 0.10, 0.20,
-- 0.30 and 0.35 under SWATINIT 0.30 in 25-28, and SGL 0.05 in 29-34.
-- Water zone (35-40).  There are no wells; the compositional flow equations
-- do not include capillary pressure yet, so over the few short time steps
-- the mobile water above the water-oil contact is not held in place.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
